, eu-west). The rollback reported as verified.\n\n- **Why v2.3.0:** It is the most recent release marked healthy. v2.3.1 and v2.3.1-rc are both unhealthy, and v2.2.9 is older.\n- **Before the rollback:** checkout-api was on v2.3.1 in every region, unhealthy, with an error rate of 0.18.\n- **Incident:** I opened SEV2 incident INC-0001, \"checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy\". It describes the rollback and the deployment history, and it paged the on-call engineer.\n\nI haven't re-checked service health since the rollback, so confirming that the error rate has dropped is still open. The incident also lists investigating the v2.3.1 failure before anyone re-releases it.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01DdzCgrgagmFGuLGuPZK714", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_015PevhJaTY3gFgM7YKCgmdF", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The most recent healthy release is v2.3.0 (v2.3.1 and v2.3.1-rc are both unhealthy). Rolling back to v2.3.0 now.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01UN8KSgSLJjhubL9WkwWVid", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0", "confidence": 0.93}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01NEBNoySnFTjxiZjKLGMNrH", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api began failing health checks after the v2.3.1 release (error rate was 0.18 across us-east, us-west, eu-west). Deployment history: v2.2.9 healthy, v2.3.0 healthy, v2.3.1-rc unhealthy, v2.3.1 unhealthy. Action taken: rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). Rollback reported VERIFIED. Next steps: confirm error rate and health recovery, and investigate the v2.3.1 failure before re-releasing.", "confidence": 0.93, "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-v2.3.1-rollback-sev2"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all three production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). The rollback reported as verified.\n\n- **Why v2.3.0:** It is the most recent release marked healthy. v2.3.1 and v2.3.1-rc are both unhealthy, and v2.2.9 is older.\n- **Before the rollback:** checkout-api was on v2.3.1 in every region, unhealthy, with an error rate of 0.18.\n- **Incident:** I opened SEV2 incident INC-0001, \"checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy\". It describes the rollback and the deployment history, and it paged the on-call engineer.\n\nI haven't re-checked service health since the rollback, so confirming that the error rate has dropped is still open. The incident also lists investigating the v2.3.1 failure before anyone re-releases it.", "type": "text"}]}]}